{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"edits\":[{\"path\":\"components/1/sound\",\"value_json\":\"[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"In Zhengzhang’s Old Chinese reconstruction, 巴 and one reading of 吧 are both *praː; the same table gives 吧 a second reading, *pʰraː. These are reconstructed forms, not recorded ancient pronunciations.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref022\\\",\\\"ref023\\\"],\\\"component_form\\\":\\\"巴\\\",\\\"component_reading\\\":\\\"*praː\\\",\\\"character_reading\\\":\\\"*praː\\\",\\\"system\\\":\\\"Old Chinese, Zhengzhang (2003) reconstruction\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"The project’s local Unihan kMandarin rows give 巴 bā and 吧 ba. This modern Mandarin pair provides a present-day reading comparison, not proof of an ancient sound relationship.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref066\\\",\\\"ref067\\\"],\\\"component_form\\\":\\\"巴\\\",\\\"component_reading\\\":\\\"bā\\\",\\\"character_reading\\\":\\\"ba\\\",\\\"system\\\":\\\"Modern Mandarin, Unihan kMandarin\\\"}]\"},{\"path\":\"components/1/sound_limitation\",\"value_json\":\"The modern Mandarin reading pair is recorded in local Unihan data and does not establish the historical phonetic relationship; the Old Chinese reconstructions are secondary table evidence, not direct ancient pronunciations.\"},{\"path\":\"components/1/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref011\\\",\\\"ref022\\\",\\\"ref023\\\",\\\"ref029\\\",\\\"ref031\\\",\\\"ref066\\\",\\\"ref067\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"learner/components/1/text\",\"value_json\":\"巴 gives 吧 its sound cue; their Mandarin readings bā and ba are similar, and historical reconstructions also show a correspondence.\"}]}"}}
